# London fare zones: a proximal map. Each character takes the fare zone
# of the nearest of 574 rail stations inside Greater London.
#
# Stations: Transport for London Unified API, StopPoint/Mode/{mode} for
#   tube, dlr, overground, elizabeth-line and national-rail (all pages),
#   downloaded 18 November 2026. https://api.tfl.gov.uk/
#   Stops of type NaptanMetroStation or NaptanRailStation, with the fare
#   zone from each stop's 'Zone' property.
#   Powered by TfL Open Data. Contains OS data (c) Crown copyright and
#   database rights 2016 and Geomni UK Map data (c) and database rights
#   [2019]. Used under TfL's open data terms (Transport Data Service
#   licence), which are based on the Open Government Licence. TfL's terms
#   page could not be reached when this deck was made, so this wording
#   has not been checked against it.
# Outline: London boroughs, ONS Local Authority Districts (December 2024)
#   BFE; river: OS Open Rivers. Source: Office for National Statistics
#   licensed under the OGL v3.0. Contains OS data (c) Crown copyright and
#   database right 2024-2026.
#
# Simplified: a station in two zones (e.g. '2+3') takes the lower one,
# the zone its fares are charged at. Stops of different modes less than
# 150 m apart are merged into one station (lowest zone kept). Only
# stations inside the Greater London boundary are used; Tramlink stops
# (no zones) are not. Three stops in London have no zone in the data
# and are left out: St Pancras International, Stratford International
# and one of two Clapham Junction entries (the other is zone 2).
# Points are ordered north to south.
# Latitude and longitude are converted to British National Grid with
# pyproj (Helmert, within a few metres). Outline simplified to 150 m,
# Thames to 60 m. Coordinates are kilometres: down from northing 202 km,
# across from easting 502.5 km; 0.2 inch per km.
